\section{Differences between census years}{

Column names follow the 2021 file, but the available columns differ between census years. The main
change is between 1996 and 2001:
\itemize{
\item 2001 to 2021 have one row per dissemination block, identified by \code{DBUID}. There is no 2001 attribute
file, the 2001 data was derived from the 2001 GeoSuite and has no total dwelling counts or block areas.
\item 1981 to 1996 have one row per enumeration area, identified by \code{EAUID}. These have different
columns, for example \code{CTCODE} instead of \code{CTUID} and no dissemination areas.
}

Identifiers are only unique within a census year, the same \code{DBUID} or \code{EAUID} in another year
does not generally refer to the same area. In 2001 and 2006 the fields for census metropolitan areas and
agglomerations, census tracts and urban areas were filled outside of those areas to match the files from
2011 on, so not all of these values are in the source. The \code{notes_en} entry of the metadata has details
